+## Jobs-to-Be-Done (JTBD)
+
+### Core Functional Job
+
+**Primary job statement**: Turn a weekly-meeting transcript into confirmed, owned, due-dated action items before follow-up is scheduled.
+
+**Job context**:
+
+- **When**: immediately after a weekly team meeting, when discussion and proposed commitments are still available in the transcript.
+- **With**: a meeting transcript, the facilitator’s knowledge of the discussion, and the team’s follow-up practices.
+- **Goal**: capture the actions the team actually intends to take and leave none eligible for reminders until accountability is confirmed.
+
+### Related Jobs
+
+1. **Review extracted proposals**: decide whether each proposed action represents a real follow-up item.
+   - Relationship: during the core job.
+
+2. **Assign accountability details**: confirm the responsible person and the due date for a chosen action.
+   - Relationship: during the core job.
+
+3. **Choose a reminder channel**: determine whether email or Slack is appropriate for the pilot.
+   - Relationship: after the core job; intentionally unresolved at this phase.
+
+### Emotional & Social Jobs
+
+**Emotional jobs**:
+
+- Feel confident that important meeting follow-up will not disappear after the call.
+- Avoid feeling responsible for chasing vague, unowned commitments.
+
+**Social jobs**:
+
+- Appear organized and fair to team members by confirming responsibility before follow-up occurs.
+- Avoid appearing to assign or remind people based on an unreviewed transcript inference.
+
+### Key Desired Outcomes (Ranked)
+
+| Priority | Outcome statement | Current pain level |
+|----------|-------------------|--------------------|
+| 1 | Minimize the likelihood that a meeting action remains unowned after review | High |
+| 2 | Minimize the time it takes to turn a transcript into reviewed actions | High |
+| 3 | Minimize the likelihood that a reminder is associated with an action lacking an owner or due date | High |
+| 4 | Increase confidence that an assigned action reflects the facilitator’s judgment | Medium |
+| 5 | Reduce the number of overdue actions that have no accountable owner | High |
+
+### Competitive Job Executors
+
+| Current solution | Strengths | Weaknesses (opportunities) |
+|------------------|-----------|-----------------------------|
+| Manual transcript or notes review | Keeps facilitator judgment in control | Slow and easy to postpone; actions can be missed |
+| Separate task lists | Familiar place to record confirmed work | Requires manually identifying and transferring actions from the meeting |
+| Verbal agreement or chat follow-up | Fast for a small number of actions | Details are scattered and ownership may remain ambiguous |
+
+### JTBD-Driven Prioritization
+
+The v1 priority is the accountability gate: extract proposals, then require facilitator review, owner confirmation, and due-date confirmation before reminder scheduling. Convenience features that bypass this gate do not serve the core job.
+
